SDL3 Libraries 3.4.18 Package for version 3.20 or higher of MorphOS system.
**************************************************************************

SDL3.LIBRARY					3.418	27.10.2026 based on SDL 3.4.18
SDL3_IMAGE.LIBRARY		3.409	07.10.2026 based on SDL3_IMAGE 3.4.9
SDL3_MIXER.LIBRARY		3.300	27.10.2026 based on SDL3_MIXER 3.3.0
SDL3_TTF.LIBRARY			3.300	07.10.2026 based on SDL3_TTF 3.3.0
SDL3_NET.LIBRARY			-		not included yet (work in progress, coming in a next release)

Library version = SDL version: VERSION = major, REVISION = minor * 100 + micro (SDL 3.4.18 -> 3.418).

Simple DirectMedia Layer
************************

What is it?
Simple DirectMedia Layer is a cross-platform development library designed to provide low level access to audio, keyboard, mouse, joystick, and graphics hardware via OpenGL/Direct3D/Metal/Vulkan. It is used by video playback software, emulators, and popular games including Valve's award winning catalog and many Humble Bundle games.

SDL 3.0 is distributed under the zlib license. This license allows you to use SDL freely in any software.

https://libsdl.org/
https://wiki.libsdl.org/


Installation:
*************

MorphOS version 3.20 is required to be installed as a minimum.
Developer: You need  new SDK 3.20!!
sdl3_ttf.library needs freetype.library 59 and harfbuzz.library 67 (system libraries).
sdl3_image.library uses system jfif.library, png.library and tiff.library (a missing one only disables its format).
sdl3_mixer.library uses vorbisfile.library (Ogg Vorbis, and the Ogg container of FLAC and Opus).
sdl3_mixer.library needs fluidsynth.library 2.601 or newer for MIDI with FluidSynth: install the
FluidSynth_2.6.1_Library package, available on MorphOS-Storage: https://www.morphos-storage.net/?find=fluidsynth
Without it, MIDI music is played by Timidity.
MIDI: timidity files are installed in LIBS:timidity, and the GeneralUser GS SoundFont (S. Christian Collins)
used by FluidSynth in LIBS:soundfonts/GeneralUser GS v1.471.sf2.

Just double-click on the Install icon and read the incremental instructions.

SDL2 and SDL3 can be installed together: sdl2*.library and sdl3*.library are different libraries.

- WARNING: it's recommended that you have a minimum 64MB graphics video (opengl features)
(if not, then it is advised that you disable "enhanced display" and reduce your screen resolution of Ambient)


SDL3 MorphOS Features:
**********************

- Shared libraries: a program and the sdl3_* libraries it uses share the same SDL state
- SDL renderer: OpenGL (TinyGL), Overlay (cgxvideo VLayer) and Software renderer are available
- Renderer can be chosen in the window menu, or with ENV:SDL3_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER (opengl, overlay, software)
- Ctrl-C/Break quits programs, also without a window
- SDL3_image: BMP, GIF, JPG, LBM, PCX, PNG, PNM, QOI, SVG, TGA, TIFF, WEBP, XCF, XPM, XV and animations (GIF, APNG, WEBP, ANI)
- SDL3_mixer: WAV, AIFF, VOC, AU, MP3, Ogg Vorbis, FLAC, Opus, MOD/XM/S3M/IT (libxmp), MIDI (FluidSynth by
  fluidsynth.library, Timidity)
- SDL3_ttf: FreeType and HarfBuzz from the system, SVG/colour emoji fonts

SDL3 MorphOS specific and limitation:
************************************

- sdl3_ttf: the OpenGL text engine (TTF_CreateGLTextEngine) is not available in the library
- Programs linked with an old SDL3 SDK (53.x glue) have to be relinked
- sdl3_mixer MIDI: seeking backwards in a MIDI file (a loop that doesn't start at the beginning) renders the
  music again from the start: a short gap while it plays. Loops from the start are immediate.

SDL3 MorphOS window menu and settings:
**************************************

Each SDL3 window has a MorphOS menu (right mouse button):
- Project: About SDL3, Iconify, Quit
- Options: Mute Sound, Low CPU Priority,
           HINT RENDER DRIVER (Default, OpenGL, Software, Overlay),
           HINT RENDER VSYNC (Default, Enabled, Disabled)

The Options are saved in ENVARC: and are used by all the SDL3 programs:
- SDL3_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER      opengl, software or overlay (empty: default renderer)
- SDL3_HINT_RENDER_VSYNC       1 (enabled) or 0 (disabled)
- SDL3_THREAD_PRIORITY_POLICY  -1: low CPU priority
They can also be set by hand: setenv SDL3_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER overlay (copy ENV:SDL3_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER
to ENVARC: to keep it after a reboot).
Debug: setenv SDL3_HINT_DEBUG 1 prints debug traces in the debug log.
The other SDL hints (SDL_xxx) are not read from ENV:, only set by the programs (SDL_SetHint).

For developers (MorphOS specific):
- Window without the MorphOS menu: SDL_CreateWindowWithProperties() with the boolean property
  "SDL.window.create.morphos.menu" set to false.
- Use an existing Intuition window: pointer property "morphos.window" (struct Window *).
- SDL_LoadObject() uses dynload.library: a module is a relocatable object built with
  gcc -noixemul -G 0 -fno-common -nostdlib -nostartfiles -r x.c -o x.so (no libc inside, it uses the program's).
  The program: -G 0 at compile and link time, only --strip-debug (the module looks its symbols up), and it
  must contain every libc function the modules need. Modules see the program's symbols, not sdl3.library's.
  The old libdll modules (separate executables) are not supported any more.

Developers:
***********

The SDK replaces the static libraries: libSDL3.a, libSDL3_image.a, libSDL3_mixer.a and libSDL3_ttf.a are
glue libraries opening the shared libraries. Link with -lSDL3_ttf -lSDL3_mixer -lSDL3_image -lSDL3 -lGL.
-mresident32 code uses the libb32 versions; the -nc ones open nothing (base set by hand): libSDL3-nc.a is the
program version (the program opens sdl3.library itself).
fd/clib/proto/ppcinline headers are included for sdl3.library and the sdl3_* libraries.
pkg-config files (sdl3, sdl3-image, sdl3-mixer, sdl3-ttf) and CMake package files are included, and libSDL3_test.a.
CMake: find_package(SDL3 REQUIRED CONFIG) then link SDL3::SDL3 (also SDL3_image::SDL3_image, SDL3_mixer::SDL3_mixer,
SDL3_ttf::SDL3_ttf, SDL3::SDL3_test, SDL3::Headers). The -static targets are not available, only the shared libraries.
The Install keeps a static libSDL3*.a already in GG:usr/local/lib: it is renamed libSDL3*_static.a.

Extras:
*******

testsprite, testgeometry, testgl, testaudioinfo, renderbench, checkkeys, testcontroller (gamepad test and mapping), testautomation (SDL3 test suite),
showimage, showanim (SDL3_image), testmixer, testaudiodecoder, testspatialization (SDL3_mixer;
testmixer --simple <file> plays a file once, without the test loops),
showfont, testapp <font.ttf> (SDL3_ttf).

GameController Readme:
**********************

SDL3 reads the gamepad mappings from ENV:gamecontrollerdb.txt (same file and format as SDL2, installed by the Install script).
To create the mapping of your own gamepad: run extras/testcontroller, click on "Setup Mapping",
press the buttons/axes asked, "Done", then "Copy" (or Ctrl-C) puts the mapping line in the clipboard: add it to ENVARC:gamecontrollerdb.txt
(and ENV:gamecontrollerdb.txt). Then any SDL2 or SDL3 game can use it.

A MorphOS community sourced database of game controller mappings is available here : https://github.com/BeWorld2018/gamecontrollerdb.txt

Please don't hesitate to participate in adding to this database, so kindly send me your working mapping(s) to add to our database. Thanks !

